---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Documentation | Twig - JSON, YAML & Data Explorer">
    <div class="docs-layout">
        <aside class="sidebar">
            <div class="toc-sticky">
                <h4>Contents</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="#introduction">Introduction</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#installation">Installation</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#core-workflow">Core Workflow</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#cli-reference">CLI Reference</a></li>
                    <li>
                        <a href="#keyboard-shortcuts">Keyboard Shortcuts</a>
                    </li>
                    <li><a href="#configuration">Configuration</a></li>
                    <li><a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </aside>

        <article class="content">
            <div class="fade-in-up">
                <section id="introduction">
                    <h1>Documentation</h1>
                    <p class="lead">
                        Twig is a high-performance, terminal-based data explorer
                        for <strong>JSON</strong> and <strong>YAML</strong>.
                        Since v3.0.0 it's a single ~4 MB static binary written
                        in Rust — drop it on any Linux, macOS, or Windows
                        machine and it runs. No Python, no runtime.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Designed for developers who work with large datasets,
                        Kubernetes manifests, logs, or complex configuration
                        files, Twig parses data into a navigable tree structure,
                        allowing for rapid inspection without ever leaving the
                        terminal.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.1s;">
                <section id="installation">
                    <h2>Installation</h2>
                    <p>
                        The recommended way to install Twig is the one-line
                        installer — it downloads the matching prebuilt binary
                        from the latest GitHub release, verifies its SHA-256
                        checksum, and installs it to <code>~/.local/bin</code>
                        (or <code>/usr/local/bin</code> when writable).
                    </p>

                    <h3>One-line installer (recommended)</h3>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://twig.wtf/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h4>Useful flags</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code># Pin a specific release
curl -fsSL https://twig.wtf/install.sh | sh -s -- --version v3.0.0

# Install to a custom directory
curl -fsSL https://twig.wtf/install.sh | sh -s -- --to /usr/local/bin

# Build from source instead of downloading
curl -fsSL https://twig.wtf/install.sh | sh -s -- --method build

# Skip the confirmation prompt
curl -fsSL https://twig.wtf/install.sh | sh -s -- --yes</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Other methods</h3>
                    <h4>Cargo</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>cargo install twig</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h4>cargo-binstall</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>cargo binstall twig</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h4>Manual download</h4>
                    <p>
                        Prebuilt <code>.tar.gz</code> archives with matching
                        <code>*.sha256</code> checksum files are available on
                        the
                        <a href="https://github.com/workdone0/twig/releases/latest">Releases page</a>
                        for Linux (x86_64, aarch64), macOS (Intel, Apple
                        Silicon), and Windows (x86_64).
                    </p>

                    <h4>Build from source</h4>
                    <p>Requires Rust 1.75 or later.</p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/workdone0/twig.git
cd twig
cargo build --release
./target/release/twig --help</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h4>Legacy Python version (≤ v2.1.4)</h4>
                    <p>
                        Older releases shipped to PyPI as
                        <code>twg</code>. That implementation is preserved on
                        the <a href="https://github.com/workdone0/twig/tree/legacy-python"><code>legacy-python</code></a>
                        branch for reference. New development happens on
                        <code>master</code>.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.2s;">
                <section id="core-workflow">
                    <h2>Core Workflow</h2>
                    <p>
                        Pass a data file to Twig. It automatically detects the
                        format (JSON or YAML), indexes it via streaming
                        ingestion, and launches the TUI.
                    </p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig data.json     # or twig config.yaml</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Repair malformed JSON</h3>
                    <p>
                        Automatically repair common errors (trailing commas,
                        unquoted keys, single quotes, NaN / Infinity) and
                        write a clean round-trippable copy.
                    </p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig --fix bad.json -o clean.json</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Benchmark streaming ingestion</h3>
                    <p>
                        Non-interactive mode that exercises the same
                        streaming pipeline the TUI uses and prints size,
                        node count, elapsed time, and throughput. Useful in
                        CI and ad-hoc perf checks.
                    </p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig --check huge.json</code></pre>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.3s;">
                <section id="cli-reference">
                    <h2>CLI Reference</h2>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig [OPTIONS] &lt;FILE&gt;</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3><code>--fix</code></h3>
                    <p>Attempt to repair malformed JSON and write a clean copy.</p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig --fix broken.json -o clean.json</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3><code>--print</code> / <code>-p</code></h3>
                    <p>Pretty-print the file to stdout with syntax highlighting.</p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig -p large.json</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3><code>--check</code></h3>
                    <p>Load the file and print size, node count, and throughput stats. Non-TUI.</p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <pre><code>twig --check huge.json</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <h3><code>--output</code> / <code>-o</code></h3>
                    <p>Write to a file instead of stdout (with <code>--print</code> or <code>--fix</code>).</p>

                    <h3><code>--indent</code> / <code>-i</code></h3>
                    <p>Indent width for pretty-printed or fixed output. Default: 2.</p>

                    <h3><code>--rebuild-db</code></h3>
                    <p>Drop the on-disk SQLite cache before loading.</p>

                    <h3><code>--version</code></h3>
                    <p>Print version and exit.</p>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.4s;">
                <section id="keyboard-shortcuts">
                    <h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>
                    <p>Twig is designed for keyboard-centric workflows.</p>

                    <div class="table-wrapper">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Context</th>
                                    <th>Action</th>
                                    <th>Key</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>General</strong></td>
                                    <td>Help / cheatsheet</td>
                                    <td><code>?</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Quit</td>
                                    <td><code>q</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Toggle theme</td>
                                    <td><code>t</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Navigation</strong></td>
                                    <td>Move selection</td>
                                    <td><code>Arrow Keys</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Drill in / expand</td>
                                    <td><code>→</code> / <code>Enter</code> / <code>l</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Step back / collapse</td>
                                    <td><code>←</code> / <code>Esc</code> / <code>h</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Jump to top / bottom</td>
                                    <td><code>g</code> / <code>G</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Smart jump (path)</td>
                                    <td><code>:</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Search</strong></td>
                                    <td>Global search</td>
                                    <td><code>/</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Next match</td>
                                    <td><code>n</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Previous match</td>
                                    <td><code>N</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Actions</strong></td>
                                    <td>Copy path</td>
                                    <td><code>c</code></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td></td>
                                    <td>Copy source slice</td>
                                    <td><code>y</code></td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.5s;">
                <section id="configuration">
                    <h2>Configuration</h2>
                    <p>
                        Twig is zero-config by default. It automatically
                        persists your settings between sessions.
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Theme</strong>: <strong>Catppuccin Mocha</strong>
                            (default) and <strong>Solarized Dark</strong> ship
                            in the box. Cycles themes with the
                            <code>t</code> key.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Config</strong>: stored at
                            <code>~/.config/twig/config.json</code> (or the
                            platform equivalent). Shared with the legacy
                            Python implementation, so theme preference carries
                            over when upgrading.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Cache</strong>: a SQLite file with an FTS5
                            virtual table, stored under the platform's cache
                            directory. Safe to delete at any time.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.6s;">
                <section id="troubleshooting">
                    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

                    <h3>Loader errors</h3>
                    <p>
                        If Twig can't parse a file, it shows the error in-app
                        (press any key to exit) and prints a colored message
                        with a <code>--fix</code> hint to stderr with exit
                        code 1, so CI pipelines fail fast.
                    </p>

                    <h3>"Database is locked" error</h3>
                    <p>
                        If Twig crashes or is killed forcefully, the SQLite
                        lock might remain. Run with <code>--rebuild-db</code>
                        to reset.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Clipboard not working</h3>
                    <p>
                        On Linux headless servers without a clipboard
                        daemon, the copy actions (<code>c</code>, <code>y</code>)
                        fall back to writing the payload to a temporary file
                        and printing its path. The TUI shows a hint when this
                        fallback fires.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </div>

            <div class="fade-in-up" style="animation-delay: 0.7s;">
                <section id="community">
                    <h2>Community</h2>
                    <p>
                        Twig is open source. If you find it useful, please
                        consider starring the project on GitHub to help others
                        discover it.
                    </p>
                    <div class="community-actions">
                        <a
                            href="https://github.com/workdone0/twig"
                            target="_blank"
                            class="btn btn-secondary"
                        >
                            ★ Star on GitHub
                        </a>
                        <a
                            href="https://buymeacoffee.com/workdone0"
                            target="_blank"
                            class="btn btn-secondary"
                        >
                            ☕ Buy me a coffee
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .docs-layout {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 240px 1fr;
        gap: 4rem;
        margin-top: 4rem;
        margin-bottom: 8rem;
    }

    /* Animations */
    @keyframes fadeInUp {
        from {
            opacity: 0;
            transform: translateY(10px);
        }
        to {
            opacity: 1;
            transform: translateY(0);
        }
    }

    .fade-in-up {
        opacity: 0;
        animation: fadeInUp 0.5s ease-out forwards;
    }

    /* Sidebar */
    .sidebar {
        position: relative;
    }
    .toc-sticky {
        position: sticky;
        top: 2rem;
        border-left: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        padding-left: 1.5rem;
    }
    .toc-sticky h4 {
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--text-primary); /* Higher contrast */
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .toc-sticky ul {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
    }
    .toc-sticky li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
    .toc-sticky a {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        font-size: 0.95rem; /* Slightly larger */
        display: block;
        transition: color 0.2s;
    }
    .toc-sticky a:hover {
        color: var(--accent-color);
    }

    /* Content Typography */
    section {
        margin-bottom: 5rem;
        scroll-margin-top: 120px;
    }

    h1 {
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        font-size: 3rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }
    .lead {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.6;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        max-width: 600px;
    }

    h2 {
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        font-size: 1.75rem;
        padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }
    h3 {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }

    p {
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.7; /* Better readability */
    }
    li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
    }

    li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
    }

    /* Table */
    .table-wrapper {
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        border-radius: 8px;
        overflow-x: auto; /* Allow horizontal scroll */
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
        max-width: 100%;
    }
    table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        min-width: 600px; /* Force scroll on small screens */
    }
    th,
    td {
        padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
        text-align: left;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    }
    /* ... existing th styles ... */
    th {
        background: var(--bg-surface);
        color: var(--text-primary);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }
    tr:last-child td {
        border-bottom: none;
    }
    td code {
        background: var(--bg-secondary); /* Fix: Use variable */
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        color: var(--text-primary);
        padding: 2px 6px;
        border-radius: 4px;
    }

    /* Inline Code in Text */
    p code,
    li code {
        background: var(--bg-secondary);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        color: var(--accent-color); /* Highlight key terms */
        padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 0.9em;
    }

    /* Community Buttons */
    .community-actions {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap; /* Allow wrapping on small screens */
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    /* Content Constraint for Grid */
    .content {
        min-width: 0; /* Allow grid item to shrink */
        max-width: 100%;
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .docs-layout {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
        .sidebar {
            display: none;
        }
    }
</style>

<!-- Global Styles for Dynamic Elements -->
<style is:global>
    /* Code Blocks - Always Dark Theme for consistency */
    .code-block {
        background: #090909;
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        border-radius: 6px;
        margin: 1.5rem 0;
        position: relative;
    }

    /* Reset global styles to prevent nesting/double borders */
    .code-block pre {
        margin: 0;
        background: transparent !important;
        border: none !important;
        padding: 1.25rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
        white-space: pre;
    }

    .code-block code {
        background: transparent !important;
        border: none !important;
        color: #e6e6e6 !important; /* Force light text in dark block */
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.9em;
        padding: 0 !important;
    }

    /* Copy Button */
    .copy-btn {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0.5rem;
        right: 0.5rem;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        border: 1px solid transparent;
        color: #aaa;
        border-radius: 4px;
        padding: 4px 8px;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        cursor: pointer;
        opacity: 0;
        transition: all 0.2s;
        z-index: 10;
    }
    /* Show on hover OR focus */
    .code-block:hover .copy-btn,
    .copy-btn:focus {
        opacity: 1;
    }

    .copy-btn:hover {
        background: #333;
        color: #fff;
        border-color: #555;
    }
    .copy-btn.copied {
        color: #4d4;
        border-color: #4d4;
    }

    /* Header Fixes */
    h3 code {
        font-size: 1.1em;
        background: var(--bg-secondary) !important; /* Use theme var */
        color: var(--accent-color) !important; /* Visible in both modes */
        padding: 0.1em 0.3em !important;
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color) !important;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-weight: 500;
    }
</style>

<script>
    // Add copy buttons to all code blocks
    document.querySelectorAll(".code-block").forEach((block) => {
        // Prevent duplicate buttons if script re-runs
        if (block.querySelector(".copy-btn")) return;

        const btn = document.createElement("button");
        btn.className = "copy-btn";
        btn.textContent = "Copy";

        btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
            const code = block.querySelector("code")?.innerText || "";
            await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.trim());

            // Feedback
            const originalText = btn.textContent;
            btn.textContent = "Copied!";
            btn.classList.add("copied");

            setTimeout(() => {
                btn.textContent = originalText;
                btn.classList.remove("copied");
            }, 2000);
        });

        block.appendChild(btn);
    });
</script>
